      <div id="p-0023" num="0022" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>5</b> </figref> is a schematic diagram of chain folding in polypropylene and the molecular level polymer structure in the folds (See “The Theory of Birefringence”, Cambridge Polymer Group, 2004, CPGAN # 014, www.campoly.com).</div>
      <div id="p-0024" num="0023" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>6</b> </figref> is SEM Micrograph of the Surface of inventive Ex. 2 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0025" num="0024" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>7</b> </figref> is SEM Micrograph of Cross Section View of Ex. 2 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0026" num="0025" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>8</b> </figref> is SEM Micrograph of the Surface of Ex. 3 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0027" num="0026" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>9</b> </figref> is SEM Micrograph of the Surface of Ex. 4 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0028" num="0027" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>10</b> </figref> is SEM Micrograph of the Surface of Ex. 5 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0029" num="0028" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>11</b> </figref> is SEM of Cross Section View of Ex. 5 Membrane.</div>
      <div id="p-0030" num="0029" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>12</b> </figref> is Side by Side Comparison of Surface SEM Micrographs of Inventive Ex. 2, 3, 4 and 5 Membranes.</div>
      <div id="p-0031" num="0030" class="description-paragraph"> <figref idrefs="DRAWINGS">FIG. <b>13</b> </figref> is SEM Surface Micrograph of CE 1.</div>
