    <div id="p-0041" num="0040" class="description-paragraph">CE 6 and <figure-callout id="5" label="CE" filenames="US12218379-20250204-D00013.png" state="{{state}}">CE</figure-callout> 5 are produced using polypropylene resins of different molecular weights and melt flow indices (mfi) which may be critical factors in the development of the crystalline lamellae regions formed during melt extrusion of the precursor membrane in a dry process.</div>
    <div id="p-0042" num="0041" class="description-paragraph">CE 6 polypropylene resin has a mfi of 5.0 g/10 minutes which is more than a 3× higher melt flow index (mfi) than the resin used to manufacture <figure-callout id="5" label="CE" filenames="US12218379-20250204-D00013.png" state="{{state}}">CE</figure-callout> 5 demonstrating a change in mfi value can have a significant effect on the development of crystalline lamellae regions and the uniformity of these crystalline lamellae regions in the microstructure of a porous separator membrane.</div>
    <heading id="h-0007">EXAMPLES</heading>
